 "area": "retina",
 "description": "Async COMMON-FATE CARVE on a 2-D az\u00d7el RETINA (the 2-D expansion of Rung 3). Objects are CARVED from the ASYNC onset-event stream (RetinalOnsetEvent, now carrying (column_index=az, row_index=el)) as maximal 8-connected COMPONENTS of firing cells sharing a coherent motion. THE 2-D CAPABILITY: two objects at the SAME azimuth but DIFFERENT elevation are ONE azimuth span to the 1-D carve (elevation collapsed) and TWO distinct 2-D components here, at their correct (az,el). The `retinal_common_fate_carve_2d` Rust task kind reduces events to one mean epoch per firing cell, groups cells into 8-connected components (a spatial gap in azimuth OR elevation separates components), fits each component's 2-D motion, and emits a fixed per-cell stride-9 layout [is_group_start, col_min, col_max, row_min, row_max, direction, speed, coherence, n_events] with each component's block written at its ANCHOR cell (smallest flat index). This rule matches every RetinalColumn cell against the done carve task and mints ONE VisionPolygon per component when coherence and n_events exceed thresholds held as DATA on a RetinaCarveParams2d node, once per cell-epoch via a carve2d_epoch guard. HONEST SCOPE: splitting two spatially-touching objects of different common fate, and 2-D motion / salience, are named follow-ons. OFF by default: the rule cannot fire unless a RetinaCarveParams2d node exists (created by the adapter only when context['retina_2d'] is set).",
 "microtheory": {
  "name": "retinal_carve_2d",
  "description": "8-connected common-fate grouping of (az,el) onset events -> VisionPolygon (az,el) regions"
 },
